"""Process-level educational comparisons, not machine-specific operating recipes."""
STEPS = {
'Representative gate dielectric growth': ('Set temperature and duration, then run the oxidation step. The Deal–Grove model computes oxide thickness and adds it to the wafer stack; thin-oxide corrections are disabled.', 'A qualified thermal oxidation sequence controls the wafer temperature, oxidizing ambient and time to grow silicon dioxide by consuming silicon at the interface. Operators verify the released recipe and equipment readiness; inspection evaluates the resulting film. Actual gate-dielectric integration may use different materials or methods, and the app model is not sufficient to qualify ultrathin gate oxides.', 'Form an insulating oxide and study how process conditions affect its modeled thickness.'),
'Incoming inspection & surface clean': ('Run the clean checkpoint; the simulator sets its particle count to zero.', 'An operator verifies lot identity and incoming condition, then runs an approved surface preparation sequence using compatible equipment. Inspection determines whether contamination requirements are met; running a clean does not prove a particle-free wafer.', 'Prepare the starting surface for subsequent interfaces and films.'),
'Verify SOI body and buried oxide': ('Read the body and buried-oxide dimensions stored in the reference SOI wafer.', 'The facility checks supplied SOI material against its specifications using appropriate metrology and supplier records. Body thickness and buried oxide are separate quantities.', 'Confirm the starting substrate matches the intended device architecture.'),
'Representative high-k gate dielectric': ('Enter a target thickness; the model adds an HfO2 layer directly to the stack.', 'A qualified process forms the gate dielectric, often using atomic layer deposition for suitable high-k films. Engineers evaluate thickness, interfaces, composition and electrical behavior. This app does not perform ALD cycle chemistry.', 'Introduce the insulating layer associated with gate control.'),
'Gate electrode deposition': ('For new bulk-planar routes, temperature, pressure, flow and elapsed time determine modeled LPCVD thickness. The FD-SOI and legacy routes use target thickness bookkeeping.', 'An operator loads the released lot and runs the approved gate-stack recipe. The actual material and deposition method depend on process integration. Film thickness, uniformity and material properties are checked; a generic silicon layer does not reproduce a modern qualified gate stack.', 'Provide material that will subsequently be patterned into a gate electrode.'),
'Coat, align, expose & develop': ('Set an overlay offset and run the alignment check. The app records nominal feature size and alignment; it does not form a physical resist image.', 'A lithography sequence coats photoresist, performs the prescribed bake steps, aligns the wafer and pattern, exposes the resist, and develops it. Inspection checks pattern quality before transfer.', 'Define where the next pattern-transfer process acts.'),
'Second pattern alignment demonstration': ('Run a second alignment check within the reference overlay window.', 'A multi-patterning scheme needs a defined sequence of masks and intermediate processing. Operators align each relevant level and inspect registration. This additional app step illustrates alignment only, not a complete multi-patterning flow.', 'Study why registration between patterning steps matters.'),
'Pattern transfer into gate electrode': ('Set source and bias RF powers. The plasma model estimates etch rate and anisotropy; the stack marks the gate film as patterned.', 'A qualified etch process removes exposed gate material while the mask protects intended features. Engineers check endpoint, selectivity and resulting dimensions/profile. The app does not calculate full evolving feature geometry.', 'Transfer the defined pattern into the electrode film.'),
'Resist strip & post-etch clean': ('Run a second clean checkpoint after pattern transfer; the simulated contamination count is reset.', 'After the mask has served its purpose, an approved strip and residue-clean sequence removes resist and etch by-products while protecting the remaining materials. Compatibility and inspection determine acceptability.', 'Remove temporary mask material and residues before later processing.'),
'Representative source/drain implant': ('Choose ion energy; the existing arsenic range model reports projected range and straggle.', 'The released implant recipe specifies species, dose, energy and other tool settings. The operator verifies the recipe and lot, while equipment delivers the ion beam under controlled conditions. Range alone does not establish dose, activated concentration or junction performance.', 'Introduce dopant into selected regions before activation processing.'),
'Raised source/drain concept demonstration': ('Enter the requested regional height; the app records it as a concept result without simulating epitaxial growth.', 'A suitable process integration may use selective epitaxial growth to form raised regions. Material, doping, selectivity and geometry are process-specific and require inspection.', 'Illustrate adding material locally in source/drain regions.'),
'Thermal activation / recovery checkpoint': ('Complete an anneal checkpoint. No dopant activation or diffusion is calculated.', 'The approved thermal cycle controls temperature history and ambient for the intended material changes, such as implant damage recovery and dopant activation. Engineers evaluate activation and unwanted redistribution.', 'Connect implantation or other prior processing with its required thermal treatment.'),
'Interlayer dielectric deposition': ('Enter a thickness target; the app adds a SiO2 layer to the stack.', 'An approved dielectric process deposits an insulating film. Coverage, thickness, defects and integration with later contacts/interconnects are evaluated.', 'Provide insulation associated with subsequent wiring levels.'),
'Dielectric planarization': ('Enter removal thickness; the app subtracts material from the top film.', 'CMP equipment uses a qualified pad/slurry and controlled mechanics to reduce topography. Inspection assesses remaining film, uniformity, defects and local effects. A thickness subtraction alone does not establish planarity.', 'Prepare a more suitable surface for later lithography and interconnect processing.'),
'Damascene interconnect pattern': ('Run another overlay check for the wiring-pattern step.', 'Lithography defines the intended openings in the dielectric using the released mask and resist process. Operators inspect alignment and pattern quality before dielectric etching.', 'Define the intended interconnect openings.'),
'Dielectric trench pattern transfer': ('Run the plasma model with dielectric chemistry assumptions; mark the dielectric as patterned.', 'A dielectric etch transfers the mask openings into the insulating material. Depth, profile, selectivity and residue control affect later metal filling.', 'Create the openings that will subsequently receive conductor material.'),
'Al interconnect deposition': ('Add the requested aluminum thickness to the stack.', 'An aluminum wiring process deposits and patterns conductor using its qualified integration sequence. This condensed app route omits important operations; adding an Al film does not create a complete connected wiring network.', 'Introduce the conductor used by this reference interconnect concept.'),
'Cu interconnect deposition': ('Add the requested copper thickness to the stack.', 'A copper damascene integration generally includes barrier/liner and seed preparation, metal fill and subsequent planarization. The operator follows the released sequence and checks fill quality. These intermediate layers and fill mechanics are omitted here.', 'Introduce conductor into the interconnect concept before overburden removal.'),
'Cu overburden polish': ('Subtract the requested amount from the top copper film.', 'A qualified copper CMP sequence removes overburden while controlling remaining structures, dishing, erosion and defects. Endpoint and post-process inspection matter; uniform subtraction cannot reproduce them.', 'Illustrate removing excess conductor after a fill operation.'),
'Final thickness, CD & defect inspection': ('Read total film thickness and particle count from simulator state, plus SOI dimensions where applicable. This step does not independently measure CD despite its route title.', 'Real inspection uses an appropriate measurement plan and calibrated methods for specified dimensions, thicknesses and defects. Engineers compare results with release criteria and review deviations. Final device qualification requires additional electrical and reliability evidence.', 'Review process evidence and decide whether further assessment is needed.'),
'Entry and carrier verification': ('Confirm the apparel, glove/footwear and carrier checkboxes to enable the route.', 'Personnel follow the facility gowning and handling procedure, verify authorization and material identity, and use compatible carriers. Checking boxes is not physical verification.', 'Establish contamination-control and identity discipline before processing.'),
}

def explanations():
    return {name:dict(simulator=v[0], real_work=v[1], purpose=v[2]) for name,v in STEPS.items()}
